Z||000000||Russ||04-30-2001||09:37 PM||||How do you repair a crack in the fender???||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||04-30-2001||10:16 PM||||I had a crack in my fender and I chose to just replace the fender- You can repair it with a sort of plastic welder but problem is, it won't stand up to anything bumping into it again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-30-2001||10:24 PM||||the fenders are so cheap, its not even worth putting bondo on one. Ask Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000003||fyerstarter||04-30-2001||10:48 PM||||Fiberglass?||||reg||1
Z||000004||PJ||04-30-2001||11:21 PM||||You can repair it better than new with two part semi-rigid urethane. This stuff is expensive, you'll need the application gun and mixing nozzles, not to mention grinders with sanding disks to prep it, and you'll have to finish sand it and prime it.  Finding one in the boneyard is a lot easier and cheaper.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||05-01-2001||12:53 AM||||Fiber Glass is not a good Idea on flexable panels!<BR>Think about it!<BR>Find a new fender and put some color on it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PAUL88GT||05-01-2001||06:15 PM||||I bought a good used fender at the Fiero Factory Swap Meet for $10.  You probably could not get the bondo or filler for that price.||||reg||1
